# CSA state — hooks append .csa/review-bypass.log and write review-gate markers
# under .csa/state/. Tracked-ignored (not just via local .git/info/exclude) so
# fresh clones stay clean when the review-gate bypass path runs. Per AGENTS
# rules 036 (no-commit-ai-config) and 062 (no-commit-log-artifacts).
.csa/

# Log artifacts (AGENTS rule 062: never track logs)
*.log

# CLAUDE.md is intentionally NOT tracked in this fork (repo owner's directive).
# It is Claude-specific AI-config, which AGENTS rule 036 (no-commit-ai-config)
# requires NOT be committed (untracking via `git rm --cached` is the compliant
# mechanism, not a violation). On disk it remains a symlink to the owner's
# ignored AI-config area, so local sessions still read it. Durable contributor
# guidance lives in CONTRIBUTING.md + docs/contributing/. Ignored here (not only
# via global excludes / .git/info/exclude) so fresh clones never re-track it.
/CLAUDE.md
